# A. sigma derivation
E[a] = 2.000000000000, Var[a] = 2.000000000000
E[c] = 1 + E[a] = 3.000000 ; E[delta] = 2 ln2 - ln3 = ln(4/3) = 0.28768207 ; C* = E[c]/E[delta] = 3/ln(4/3) = 10.428178
Var(c - C* delta) = 2 (1 - C* ln2)^2 = 77.582508 ; / E[delta] = 269.6814 ; sigma = 16.4220
direct numeric Var(c - C* delta) = 77.582508 (mean of c - C* delta = 2.258e-16, should be 0)
Mazur 523/50 = 10.4600 ; ratio to C* = 1.003051 ; i.e. 0.305% above C*
renewal-reward CLT (e.g. Asmussen, Applied Probability and Queues, VI.3; Smith 1955):
  cycles (delta_i, c_i) iid, N(t) = #cycles with cumulative delta <= t, R(t) = sum c_i:
  (R(t) - r t)/sqrt(t) -> N(0, Var(c - r delta)/E delta), r = E c / E delta.  Here t = ln n.

# E. Lagarias-Weiss constant from the T-map word count (odd fraction p, gamma T-steps per ln n)
gamma_BP (T-steps) = 41.677648, odd fraction p = 0.609090 ; ordinary-step version gamma (1+p) = 67.0631
typical T-steps per ln n = 2/ln(4/3) = 6.95212 ; ordinary = 3/ln(4/3) = 10.42818

