# C. Proposition F constant and entropy saving
C_F = (1 + (1 + log2 3)/2)/ln 2 = 3.307351
tau >= k0 + d0 + log2(m0) with m0 >= 3^d0  ->  tau >= k0 + d0 (1 + log2 3) ; with d0 = p k0, k0 ~ log2 X: tau/ln X >= (1 + p (1 + log2 3))/ln 2
  p = 0.50 : lower bound tau/ln X >= 3.3074 ; #{words of weight <= p k0} <= 2^(k0 H2(p)), H2 = 1.00000, exponent saving c = 0.00000
  p = 0.49 : lower bound tau/ln X >= 3.2701 ; #{words of weight <= p k0} <= 2^(k0 H2(p)), H2 = 0.99971, exponent saving c = 0.00029
  p = 0.48 : lower bound tau/ln X >= 3.2328 ; #{words of weight <= p k0} <= 2^(k0 H2(p)), H2 = 0.99885, exponent saving c = 0.00115
  p = 0.45 : lower bound tau/ln X >= 3.1209 ; #{words of weight <= p k0} <= 2^(k0 H2(p)), H2 = 0.99277, exponent saving c = 0.00723
  p = 0.40 : lower bound tau/ln X >= 2.9344 ; #{words of weight <= p k0} <= 2^(k0 H2(p)), H2 = 0.97095, exponent saving c = 0.02905
  p = 0.30 : lower bound tau/ln X >= 2.5615 ; #{words of weight <= p k0} <= 2^(k0 H2(p)), H2 = 0.88129, exponent saving c = 0.11871
so for C < C_F choose p < 1/2 with (1 + p(1+log2 3))/ln2 > C: count of n in [X/2,X) with tau < C ln n is <= 2 * 2^(k0 H2(p)) = O(X^(1-c)).
entropy bound log2(sum_{j<=pk} C(k,j)) - k H2(p) max over k < 400, p <= 1/2 : 0.000000 (must be <= 0)

